    "final_answer": "Upgraded `payout_sync.py` to the v2 export API.\n\nChanges:\n- Uses `GET /v2/payouts` with `cursor` pagination.\n- Follows cursors until `drained: true`, rather than assuming a short page is the end.\n- Deduplicates overlapping windows by payout `id`, preserving creation order.\n- Retries `429` responses using `Retry-After`, resending the identical request.\n- Restarts the export without a cursor on `400 invalid_cursor`, still deduplicating.\n- Keeps the existing CLI and output format unchanged.\n\nVerification against `http://the VM's public address:18080`:\n- Synced all **2,431** payouts from v2.\n- Output was **exactly identical** to v1, in the same order, with **2,431 unique IDs**.\n- Also tested a local mock covering overlapping windows, a `429`, and an expired cursor; all payouts still appeared exactly once.",
